From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luke Craig <lacraig3@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 22:26:32 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] target/loongarch: migrate the constant timer

The constant timer's deadline lives only in the CPU's QEMUTimer; TVAL is
computed from it. The timer was not in the vmstate, so after a load TCFG
says the timer is enabled but nothing is armed, and a guest waiting in
idle is never woken: a plain savevm/loadvm leaves the guest frozen, and
record/replay stalls at icount 679.

Migrate the QEMUTimer in a "cpu/timer" subsection, sent whenever TCG is
in use. It is sent even when the timer is stopped, because loading a
stopped timer must also stop a running one.

The CPU's common state goes the same way: dc->vmsd is set, so
vmstate_cpu_common is never registered for this CPU, and halted and
interrupt_request are lost. A snapshot taken while an interrupt is
pending loads with ESTAT showing it but no CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD request;
the line is already high, nothing raises it again, and a guest in idle
never wakes (a slow host takes snapshots in that window often). Migrate
it too, in a "cpu/common" subsection under the same condition.

SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later

Origin: new
---
 target/loongarch/machine.c | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 46 insertions(+)

diff --git a/target/loongarch/machine.c b/target/loongarch/machine.c
index 931a5ca5baa51102eb7a0db9e3afddafdc3325bb..7e68b1a980a47919c81ea45ac37ef8736cf8e4b2 100644
--- a/target/loongarch/machine.c
+++ b/target/loongarch/machine.c
@@ -205,6 +205,50 @@ static const VMStateDescription vmstate_tlb = {
         VMSTATE_END_OF_LIST()
     }
 };
+
+static bool timer_needed(void *opaque)
+{
+    /* Also when idle: loading a stopped timer must stop a running one. */
+    return tcg_enabled();
+}
+
+/*
+ * The constant timer's deadline lives only in cpu->timer (TVAL is computed
+ * from it): without it a restored guest waiting in idle for its next tick
+ * is never woken.
+ */
+static const VMStateDescription vmstate_timer = {
+    .name = "cpu/timer",
+    .version_id = 1,
+    .minimum_version_id = 1,
+    .needed = timer_needed,
+    .fields = (const VMStateField[]) {
+        VMSTATE_TIMER(timer, LoongArchCPU),
+        VMSTATE_END_OF_LIST()
+    }
+};
+
+/*
+ * dc->vmsd is set, so vmstate_cpu_common is not registered for this CPU and
+ * halted and interrupt_request were never migrated. ESTAT comes back with an
+ * interrupt pending but the CPU with no CPU_INTERRUPT_HARD request: the line
+ * is already high, nothing raises it again, and a guest in idle sleeps on.
+ */
+static bool common_needed(void *opaque)
+{
+    return tcg_enabled();
+}
+
+static const VMStateDescription vmstate_common = {
+    .name = "cpu/common",
+    .version_id = 1,
+    .minimum_version_id = 1,
+    .needed = common_needed,
+    .fields = (const VMStateField[]) {
+        VMSTATE_STRUCT(parent_obj, LoongArchCPU, 0, vmstate_cpu_common, CPUState),
+        VMSTATE_END_OF_LIST()
+    }
+};
 #endif
 
 /* LoongArch CPU state */
@@ -285,6 +329,8 @@ const VMStateDescription vmstate_loongarch_cpu = {
         &vmstate_lasx,
 #if defined(CONFIG_TCG) && !defined(CONFIG_USER_ONLY)
         &vmstate_tlb,
+        &vmstate_timer,
+        &vmstate_common,
 #endif
         &vmstate_lbt,
         &vmstate_msgint,
